# What is not pushed.
#
# Worth being thorough here rather than relying on nothing stray ever appearing: the release stages
# this repository with `git add -A`, so anything sitting in the working tree at publish time goes to
# the deploy. Note what is deliberately absent — `public/client` is build output and IS committed,
# because Vercel builds from the pushed commit and never runs the client's Gradle build.

/node_modules
/dist
/.vercel

# Android build output. The density mipmaps are generated from `android/art` by
# `android/tools/make-icons.sh` on every build, so committing them would leave a second copy to keep
# in step. `mipmap-anydpi-v26` is hand-written and stays.
/android/.gradle
/android/build
/android/app/build
/android/local.properties
/android/app/src/main/res/mipmap-*dpi/

# Local configuration and credentials.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editors and tooling.
/.idea
/.vscode
*.swp
*.tsbuildinfo

# Logs.
*.log

# Operating system leavings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
